g room, the organization name, the department name, and the difference between the access level of the room and the average access level for that department. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4773\", \"name\": \"Level-5 Organization Space Units Matched with Floor-2 Rooms via Space Unit Code and HR Department Attributes\", \"category\": \"Facility Space and Organization Hierarchy Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each organization with an organization level of 5 and for rooms on floor 2 that are associated via space unit code, show the organization name, organization key, description, space unit, space unit key, the average organization key within each organization key group ordered by space unit key, the building room, space usage, the HR org unit title, the department name, the minimum access level in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the building component, and the HR org unit level and department code for each room, ordered by organization name and building room. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4162\", \"name\": \"Room 21E Windowed Min Square Footage Matched with Access-Level-1 Rooms of the Same Space Unit Code\", \"category\": \"Facility Space Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For rooms with a room number of '21E' and for rooms with an access level of 1 in the same space unit code, show the building room, room square footage, building component, space usage, the minimum room square footage in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by building key, the warehouse load date from both the SPACE_DETAIL and SPACE_USAGE tables, the floor, space unit code, space unit name, the average floor within each space unit code group, and the total number of rooms per space unit code. List the results ordered by building room and floor. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}]}"
