b)`).\n- **dw_3916, dw_4162, dw_4271, dw_4033, dw_4773** — All access-level-per-space-unit precedents; every one joins `SPACE_UNIT t0 JOIN ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD t1 ON t0.SPACE_UNIT_CODE = t1.SPACE_UNIT_CODE` and filters/groups on `t1.ACCESS_LEVEL`, counting rooms with `COUNT(*)` grouped by space unit (dw_3916: `GROUP BY t0.SPACE_UNIT HAVING COUNT(*) > 1`; dw_4162 `RoomCounts`: `SELECT SPACE_UNIT_CODE, COUNT(*) … WHERE ACCESS_LEVEL = 1 GROUP BY SPACE_UNIT_CODE`).\n\n**Concepts**\n- **concept_space_unit_dimension** — SPACE_UNIT vs SPACE_UNIT2; decision guide: \"Counting rooms per space unit … Join SPACE_DETAIL to SPACE_UNIT on SPACE_UNIT_KEY (preferred for full coverage)\"; SPACE_UNIT preferred over SPACE_UNIT2 for coverage.\n- **concept_room_space_inventory** — SPACE_DETAIL vs FCLT_ROOMS vs FAC_ROOMS vs ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD; decision guide: \"Room analysis by floor, space usage text, or **access level linked to space units** … Use ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD: it links rooms to SPACE_UNIT via SPACE_UNIT_CODE.\"\n\n**Column Concepts**\n- **column_concept_access_level** — Room-level ACCESS_LEVEL exists in FCLT_ROOMS, FAC_ROOMS, ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD (values 0–3). Decision guide: \"Room access level analysis combined with … space unit / HR org unit linkage → Use ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD.ACCESS_LEVEL.\"\n- **column_concept_space_unit_key** — SPACE_UNIT_KEY links SPACE_DETAIL↔SPACE_UNIT; ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD instead links via SPACE_UNIT_CODE.\n- **column_concept_building_room** — Room identifier in SPACE_DETAIL/FCLT_ROOMS/ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD; cross-table text matching unreliable (only ~2,666 of 9,332/9,872 values overlap), so single-feed counting is required.\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n- `ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD` graph neighbors: joins → SPACE_UNIT (via SPACE_UNIT_CODE), FCLT_ORGANIZATION & HR_ORG_UNIT (via HR_ORG_UNIT_ID); incoming concept → concept_room_space_inventory; incoming column_concepts → building_room, access_level. `metrics_by_table` → 5 metrics (dw_3916, dw_4033, dw_4162, dw_4271, dw_4773), all access-level room analyses.\n- `SPACE_UNIT` graph neighbors: joins → FCLT_ORGANIZATION (outgoing); incoming from SPACE_DETAIL (SPACE_UNIT_KEY), ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD (SPACE_UNIT_CODE), FCLT_ROOMS, SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE; concept → concept_space_unit_dimension; column_concepts → space_unit_key, facility_organization_key, dlc_key.\n- dw_2616 lineage: SPACE_DETAIL + SPACE_USAGE only (no access level available there).\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix (room-source candidates for \"rooms per space unit with access level\")**\n\n| Dimension | ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD | SPACE_DETAIL | FCLT_ROOMS / FAC_ROOMS |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Space-unit linkage | `SPACE_UNIT_CODE` → SPACE_UNIT (documented join; used in 5 metrics) | `SPACE_UNIT_KEY` → SPACE_UNIT (documented join) | None — organization keys only (column lists) |\n| Room ACCESS_LEVEL | Yes, 0–3 (column def) | **Absent** (column list) | Yes, but no space-unit link |\n| Granularity | one row per room record | one row per assigned room | one row per room |\n| Fan-out risk | join on SPACE_UNIT_CODE, 1:1 dimension | join on SPACE_UNIT_KEY, 1:1 | n/a for this task |\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness**\n- Required: room-level ACCESS_LEVEL filter (≥1) **and** per-space-unit grouping.\n  - ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD + SPACE_UNIT: SUPPORTED (both columns exist; documented join).\n  - SPACE_DETAIL + SPACE_UNIT: NOT-SUPPORTED (no ACCESS_LEVEL column).\n  - FCLT_ROOMS/FAC_ROOMS: NOT-SUPPORTED (no space-unit key; only organization attribution).\n- Required: space unit name → SPACE_UNIT.SPACE_UNIT: SUPPORTED (SPACE_UNIT2 also SUPPORTED but is a strict subset — coverage risk).\n- Required: \"greater than the average … per space unit\" → two-level aggregation: SUPPORTED via CTE + scalar AVG subquery (dw_2616 precedent pattern).\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring**\n- \"space unit name\" → `SPACE_UNIT.SPACE_UNIT` (column desc: \"Name of the space unit\").\n- \"number of rooms assigned to it\" → `COUNT(*)` over ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD rows joined per space unit (eac